# Walkthrough: MathViz Architecture Refactor

I have completed a comprehensive restructuring of the MathViz codebase. This refactor transforms the application from a monolithic, state-duplicated structure into a clean, modular, and maintainable architecture.

## Changes Overview

### 1. Monolith Decomposition
The formerly ~2000-line `MathVisualizer.tsx` has been broken down into a suite of specialized, reusable components.

- **[MathVisualizer.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/MathVizTutor/src/components/math-visualizer/MathVisualizer.tsx)**: Now a lean ~150-line orchestrator.
- **New Modular Components**:
  - [WelcomeScreen.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/MathVizTutor/src/components/math-visualizer/WelcomeScreen.tsx)
  - [ShortcutsOverlay.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/MathVizTutor/src/components/math-visualizer/ShortcutsOverlay.tsx)
  - [QuickLessonPicker.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/MathVizTutor/src/components/math-visualizer/QuickLessonPicker.tsx)
  - [StepNarrative.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/MathVizTutor/src/components/math-visualizer/StepNarrative.tsx)
  - [LessonControls.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/MathVizTutor/src/components/math-visualizer/LessonProgressBar.tsx) (and others)

### 2. Unified Canvas Engine
I have replaced the simplified `MathCanvas.tsx` with the advanced rendering logic previously trapped inside the monolith.

- **[MathCanvas.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/MathVizTutor/src/components/math-visualizer/MathCanvas.tsx)**:
  - **Dynamic Auto-Framing**: Automatically calculates the bounding box of mathematical elements to ensure perfect centering and zero clipping.
  - **Advanced Rendering**: 3B1B-inspired serif typography, staggered entry animations, and label collision avoidance.
  - **Store Integration**: Directly subscribes to the Zustand store for coordinate and zoom state.

### 3. Centralized State & Utils
- **[utils.ts](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/MathVizTutor/src/lib/utils.ts)**: Centralized logic for `flattenSteps`, `totalSteps`, and `totalElements`.
- **Zustand Store**: The app now uses `useMathVizStore` as the single source of truth for navigation, playback, and visibility states, eliminating data synchronization bugs.

## Verification Results

### Code Integrity
- All imports and exports have been verified for correctness.
- Shared utilities and components are correctly typed according to `lesson-types.ts`.

### Visual Quality
- The "Dark Editorial" aesthetic is preserved and enhanced by the unified rendering logic in the new `MathCanvas`.
- Typography legibility for math labels is improved through serif font standardization in the canvas engine.

> [!NOTE]
> The codebase is now significantly easier to extend. New lessons or visualization types can be added by modifying the modular components or the unified `MathCanvas` without touching the main orchestrator.
